<title>JAPAN: Fourth session in Hamanaka trial set for May 8.</title>
<headline>Fourth session in Hamanaka trial set for May 8.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The fourth hearing in the trial of former Sumitomo Corp copper trader Yasuo Hamanaka has been tentatively set for May 8, one of Hamanaka's lawyers said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Hamanaka faces forgery and fraud charges in connection with an estimated $2.6 billion in losses allegedly run up over a 10-year period from unauthorised trades. He has already pleaded guilty to the two charges.</p>
</text>
